  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/Ewy4UEuhUhsQzNd2LMeUeZtf-lRvUZmlxyeeoAaILiE.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\nAcetic acid is most acidic as its conjugte base has equivalent Resonating structure followed by para-nitrophenol. Ethanol is less acidic then para-nitrophenol as conjugate base of p-nitrophenol is resonance stablized but not ethoxide $\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{O}\\right)$ Also electronegativity of carbon is lesser than oxygen, hence acetylene is less acidic.",
